<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Cochuah</h1><p class="st-meta">1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.) · capital Tihosuco</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maya province of eastern Yucatán centred on Tihosuco, conquered in 1544, whose region later became the cradle of the Caste War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Cochuah emerged after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-mayapan">League of Mayapan</a> around 1441. It lay in the forests of east-central Yucatán, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintana-roo">Quintana Roo</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tihosuco">Tihosuco</a> and Ichmul among its main towns.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Colonial sources describe Cochuah as a warlike province whose towns were governed by local lords. Its people farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and traded with the coastal provinces. Little else is recorded of its institutions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-pacheco">Gaspar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melchor-pacheco">Melchor Pacheco</a> conquered Cochuah in 1544 with great violence, and it became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-yucatan">Province of Yucatán</a>. In 1847 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste-war-of-yucatan">Caste War of Yucatán</a>, a long Maya uprising, broke out at nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepich">Tepich</a> and centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tihosuco">Tihosuco</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cochuah.jpg" alt="Cochuah" width="320" height="233"><figcaption>Image: Jaontiveros · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cacicazgos_mayas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tihosuco</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yucatec Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cochuah province</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=cochuah" aria-label="Cochuah on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2298 1430 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cochuah lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2618 1686L2591 1670M2618 1686L4910 989M2618 1686L2590 1658"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2591 1670h0M4910 989h0M2590 1658h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2618 1686h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2618 1686h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tihosuco. <a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=cochuah">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
